---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="WasmStore's privacy policy explains browser-local preferences, contact email drafts, third-party game links, advertising, cookies, and your choices." path="/privacy">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">PIXEL ARCADE · YOUR PRIVACY</div><h1>PRIVACY <span class="gradient-text">POLICY</span></h1><p>Last updated: October 17, 2026 · Plain-language information about data and choices.</p></div></section>
  <article class="prose wrap legal-page">
    <p class="legal-kicker">PRIVACY NOTES / READ BEFORE YOU PLAY</p>
    <p>This Privacy Policy describes the general way WasmStore is designed to work. The site is a game-discovery directory that links to projects and services operated by others. The actual data handled during a visit can depend on the hosting configuration, advertising scripts, embedded services, browser settings, and the external game or website you choose to open. We aim to describe these distinctions clearly and update this page when material features change.</p>
    <h2>1. Information you choose to provide</h2><p>If you use the contact form, the form prepares an email draft in your own email application. It includes the name, email address, topic, and message you enter. The static form does not itself transmit that information to a WasmStore form server; you review the draft and decide whether to send it. Once you send an email, your email provider and the recipient may process and retain it according to their own practices.</p><p>Please do not send passwords, payment information, government identifiers, or sensitive personal details that are not needed to handle your request.</p>
    <h2>2. Preferences stored in your browser</h2><p>Features such as favorites, recently played items, or the last selected surprise game may use browser local storage so they can work between visits on the same device. These preferences are stored by your browser for this site and are not, by themselves, submitted to WasmStore by those local features. Anyone with access to your browser profile may be able to see or clear this data. You can remove it using your browser's site-data or storage settings; doing so may reset saved preferences.</p>
    <h2>3. Basic technical information and hosting</h2><p>When you visit a website, the hosting or delivery infrastructure may process technical request information such as IP address, request time, requested path, browser or device details, and security logs. The precise information, retention period, and access controls depend on the hosting provider and deployed configuration. This policy does not promise a particular retention period where that information has not been verified.</p>
    <h2>4. Third-party games, embeds, and outbound links</h2><p>WasmStore listings can link to third-party demos, source repositories, project pages, video services, or other websites. When you open an external link or load a third-party embed, that provider may receive technical data, set or read cookies, or process information under its own terms and privacy policy. We do not control those services. Review the provider's policy before using a service if you have concerns.</p>
    <h2>5. Advertising, cookies, and similar technologies</h2><p>The site may be supported by advertising. If advertising scripts are enabled, advertising partners may use cookies, device identifiers, local storage, IP address, or similar technologies to deliver, measure, limit, or personalize ads, subject to the partner's configuration and applicable law. The providers and technologies actually active can change; consult the notices shown by the deployed site and your browser controls. Where consent or opt-out controls are legally required, they should be configured for the services and regions in which the site operates.</p>
    <h2>6. Analytics and measurement</h2><p>Analytics tools, if enabled in the deployed version, may collect usage and technical events to help understand site performance and navigation. We do not claim that a specific analytics provider is active unless it is identified in the live configuration. This section should be updated whenever analytics services are added, removed, or materially changed.</p>
    <h2>7. Comments and community services</h2><p>Commenting or other community features may be provided by a third party if enabled. That provider may collect account details, comments, cookies, or other information under its own policies. If a feature is not active on the page you visit, you do not need to submit information to it. Check the relevant provider's terms before creating an account or posting publicly.</p>
    <h2>8. Children's privacy</h2><p>WasmStore is a general-interest directory, not a service designed to request sensitive personal information from children. Parents and guardians should supervise children's use of external games and services, which may have different age ratings and data practices. If you believe personal information has been submitted inappropriately, contact us with enough detail to identify the issue, without sending additional sensitive information.</p>
    <h2>9. International processing and third-party policies</h2><p>Hosting, advertising, and external game services may operate in countries different from yours. Any information handled by those providers may therefore be subject to their locations, contracts, and legal obligations. Their privacy notices explain their own processing practices.</p>
    <h2>10. Your choices</h2><ul><li>Use your browser settings to clear local storage and site data.</li><li>Choose not to open an external game or embed.</li><li>Use available advertising or cookie controls where provided.</li><li>Contact us to ask a privacy question or raise a concern.</li></ul>
    <h2>11. Data security and retention</h2><p>No website or internet transmission can be guaranteed perfectly secure. Email messages may remain in sender, recipient, or provider systems after delivery. Local preferences remain in your browser until removed or cleared. Retention for hosting, advertising, and external services is controlled by the relevant provider and its configuration.</p>
    <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2><p>We may revise this page when the directory, integrations, or applicable requirements change. The “Last updated” date indicates the most recent material revision made to this page. Please review it periodically if you use the site regularly.</p>
    <h2>13. Contact</h2><p>For privacy questions, contact <a href={'mailto:'+site.contactEmail}>{site.contactEmail}</a> or use the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>. Please identify the relevant page or feature and describe your concern without including unnecessary personal information.</p>
    <p class="legal-note"><strong>Transparency note:</strong> This policy is a description of the site's intended behavior, not a guarantee that every third-party service follows the same practices. The live provider configuration should be checked whenever scripts, ads, embeds, or analytics change.</p>
  </article>
  <style>.legal-page{max-width:900px;padding-top:12px;padding-bottom:64px;line-height:1.8}.legal-page .legal-kicker{font:700 11px/1.5 var(--font-pixel);letter-spacing:.08em;color:#6b55d8}.legal-page h2{font-family:var(--font-pixel);font-size:clamp(18px,2vw,24px);line-height:1.4;margin-top:34px;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--ink);text-transform:uppercase}.legal-page p,.legal-page li{font-size:16px}.legal-page a{color:#5b43c6;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:3px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.legal-page a:hover{color:#d73569}.legal-note{background:#fff;padding:18px;border:2px solid var(--ink);box-shadow:5px 5px 0 var(--ink);margin-top:30px}@media(max-width:600px){.legal-page{padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px}.legal-page p,.legal-page li{font-size:15px}.legal-page h2{font-size:17px}}</style>
</BaseLayout>